{
  "id": "18705_kieuseru",
  "headword": "{消|き}え{失|う}せる",
  "reading": "きえうせる",
  "romaji": "kieuseru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb-ichidan",
  "gloss": "to vanish; to disappear completely",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "ichidan",
    "stem": "{消|き}え{失|う}せ"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to vanish; to disappear completely",
      "explanation": "To disappear without a trace. Stronger and more emphatic than simply {消|き}える. Can also be used as a harsh command meaning 'get lost.'"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "18705_kieuseru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{霧|きり}が{消|き}え{失|う}せた。",
      "english": "The fog vanished completely.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "18705_kieuseru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{希望|きぼう}が{消|き}え{失|う}せてしまった。",
      "english": "All hope vanished.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "18705_kieuseru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{夢|ゆめ}から{覚|さ}めると、さっきまでの{幸|しあわ}せな{気持|きも}ちが{消|き}え{失|う}せていた。",
      "english": "When I woke from the dream, the happy feeling from moments ago had completely vanished.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound verb from {消|き}える (to disappear) and {失|う}せる (to be lost/vanish). Emphasizes completeness of disappearance compared to {消|き}える alone. In imperative form ({消|き}え{失|う}せろ), it becomes a very harsh way to tell someone to get lost. Intransitive verb. Collocations: {痕跡|こんせき}が{消|き}え{失|う}せる (traces vanish), {不安|ふあん}が{消|き}え{失|う}せる (anxiety disappears).",
